N3PP - Unofficial Nura 3rd-Party Ports


# About

This is an unofficial Nura 3rd party repository created by [LogicalErzor](https://nura.eco/team/#rudraksha-gupta-logicalerzor). Think of this as the AUR, but for Nura.

This project is aimed as a catch all for device ports and packages that can't be upstreamed to Nura or elsewhere. Examples include:
- AI usage for Nura's device ports
- Proprietary software
- Experimental software


# How to Use

1. You must have run `pmbootstrap init` and git cloned this repository before proceeding. Make sure pmbootstrap, pmaports, and n3pp are up to date and have no uncommitted changes. These are the aliases we will use, so feel free to replace these paths with your own:
```sh
PMAPORTS=~/nura/pmaports
N3PP=~/nura/n3pp
MERGED=~/nura/pmaports-merged
```

To use N3PP
```sh
mkdir -p "$N3PP/.overlay-work" "$MERGED"
sudo mount -t overlay n3pp -o "lowerdir=$PMAPORTS,upperdir=$N3PP/overlay,workdir=$N3PP/.overlay-work" "$MERGED"
pmbootstrap config aports "$MERGED"
```

To undo:
```sh
pmbootstrap config aports "$PMAPORTS"
sudo umount -R "$MERGED"
```

You can then use any pmbootstrap commands you like. Be careful with git commands.


